    "created_at": "2019-03-29T21:37:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-03-29T21:37:20Z",
    "body": "I think a fix could be to remove the `src` checks there and just consider the two cases of the current image being available or not, for each of (empty alt, non-empty alt, missing alt).\r\n\r\n#images-3 would work OK as-is, but I think it's not ideal. In particular, \"the user agent does not expect this to change\" is very unclear, especially for responsive images (the next image can very well be available!).",
